# LEGION 04
# there is no image here and there never was.

A file name is a label a human typed. It is a suggestion. The actual
type is decided by what the first few bytes say, and nothing on this
machine is obliged to agree with the extension.

A real PNG starts with the bytes 89 50 4E 47. This one starts with a
hash and a space, because it is a text file wearing a costume.

Last one: 05_ghost. It is a program, and it has nothing to say out
loud, so do not bother running it. Programs are full of text that is
never printed, and the command that pulls all of it out at once is
called strings. More than one thing in there looks like a code.
Only one of them is not making excuses.
